  "preamble": "Fortition of the labio-velar glide [w] to the voiced bilabial stop [b]. In the transition from Middle Persian to New Persian, word-initial w- became b- (alongside a gw- > g- outcome in other words): Middle Persian wād 'wind' and wahār 'spring' became bād and bahār. Independently, Proto-Dravidian initial *w- became b- in Kannada and Tulu, while Tamil, Malayalam and Telugu keep v-.",
